# Luna Shopper — shared local development env (plan 0002, section 1 and 2).
#
# Copy this file (next to it) to apps/luna-shopper-backend/.env.luna-shopper-backend:
#
#   cp apps/luna-shopper-backend/.env.luna-shopper-backend.example apps/luna-shopper-backend/.env.luna-shopper-backend
#
# Only the three variables common to every service live here. Each service ALSO
# reads its own apps/luna-shopper-backend/<svc>/.env for its specific vars — copy each
# service's .env.example there too. `nx serve` runs from the workspace root, so
# both this file and the per service ones are found relative to the root, with
# the per service file taking precedence.
#
# It is deliberately NOT the bare `.env` (which Nx auto loads into every task);
# only the Luna services' @nestjs/config reads it. This file (and every
# apps/luna-shopper-backend/<svc>/.env) is git ignored; only the .example files are
# committed. Nothing secret ships in an image or build arg.

NATS_URL=nats://localhost:4222
LOG_LEVEL=debug
# Browser origins allowed through CORS (comma separated) — the shell dev server:
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200

# --- Telemetry (plan 0016) ---------------------------------------------------
# The telemetry variables deliberately do NOT live in this file. They belong in
# each service's own apps/luna-shopper-backend/<svc>/.env, and the reason is
# load bearing rather than cosmetic:
#
# The OpenTelemetry SDK starts before Nest does (plan 0016, section 4.1), so it
# can only read `process.env`. This file's custom name is known to @nestjs/config
# and nothing else, so a variable put here arrives long after the SDK has already
# decided it is switched off. Nx *does* load `{projectRoot}/.env` into the
# environment of that project's tasks, which is why the per service file works.
#
# See each service's .env.example for the block, or just run luna-slot.sh /
# luna-slot.ps1, which writes it with this slot's collector port.

# --- One time setup: the shared dev JWT keypair ------------------------------
# Every service reads the key from a file (its .env points at
# apps/luna-shopper-backend/secrets/jwt.*), so no PEM blob ever lives in a .env. Generate
# a throwaway dev pair once, from the repo root (never reuse in the cluster;
# production keys are Kubernetes Secrets):
#
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 \
#     -out apps/luna-shopper-backend/secrets/jwt.key
#   openssl pkey -in apps/luna-shopper-backend/secrets/jwt.key -pubout \
#     -out apps/luna-shopper-backend/secrets/jwt.pub
#
# The whole apps/luna-shopper-backend/secrets/ directory is git ignored (keeps .gitkeep).
